{"abstract":"Video game designers often view confusion as undesirable, yet it is inevitable, as new players must adapt to new interfaces and mechanics in an increasingly varied and innovative game market, which is more popular than ever. Research suggests that confusion can contribute to a positive experience, potentially motivating players to learn. The state of confusion in video games should be further investigated to gain more insight into the learning experience of play and how it affects the player experience. In this article, we design a study to collect learning-related affects for users playing a game prototype that intentionally confuses the player. We assess the gathered affects against a complex learning model, affirming that, in specific instances, the player experience aligns with the learning experiences. Moreover, we identify correlations between these affects and the Player Experience Inventory constructs, particularly concerning flow experiences.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Volden, Thomas Vase Schultz","Jarma Montoya, Oleg","Scirea, Marco","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828170"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affect","Confusion","FLOW","Learning","Player Experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the dynamics of affect during play and the role of confusion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/112428043/CoG_2025_Short_On_the_dynamics_of_affective_states_during_play_and_the_role_of_confusion_4_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828170","ids":["itu-9ce701a3-057e-4657-a53b-4acc1f6f9cac"],"keyword":["affect","confusion","flow","learning","player experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D808702DF98233A619ACCA0DCA4DB64C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/112428043/CoG_2025_Short_On_the_dynamics_of_affective_states_during_play_and_the_role_of_confusion_4_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, brAIn lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Vase Schultz","key":"voldenpau","last":"Volden","locid":"7e884581-3d40-42e6-af12-453e052c9c87","name":"Volden, Thomas Vase Schultz","orcid":"0009-0009-2177-5482","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Oleg","key":"jarmamontoyapau","last":"Jarma Montoya","name":"Jarma Montoya, Oleg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","name":"Scirea, Marco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burel